      "content": "<h3>4. size(), isEmpty() and clear()</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>int size();  boolean isEmpty();  void clear()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the count / whether empty / nothing</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1) / O(1) / O(capacity)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Count the elements, test for none, or remove all of them.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> <code>clear()</code> empties the table but keeps its capacity, so the set does not shrink. Clearing a set that once held millions of elements leaves a big, empty table behind; create a new set if memory matters.</p>",
